    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://edamontology.org/topic___Supervised_learning">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/bio"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/imaging"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/topics"/>
        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Work comments:
28th August 2018

within supervised learning there could be ‘regression’ and ‘classification’
joakim.lindblad
20th March 2019

It&apos;s a good question how deep to go. Currently we&apos;re going less deep within Topics (which are rather broad fluffy) than the operations. Thus I added a seeAlso to the operation</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Supervised learning</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/operation_2423"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/operation_2990"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supervised_learning"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


