        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/topic__ReQzVVVh0IPyN0c1V5wQVO"/>
        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Work comments:
Xavier Heiligenstein
20th March 2019

This contains the sub categories: microtomy, ultra-microtomy, blotting, vibrating blade sectioning, cryo-microtomy, oscillating, ablation

Matthia.Karreman
20th March 2019

Examples of sample thinning

    blotting (as in vitrobot)
    microtomy (ultra-, cryo- (ultra), vibratome, oscilating knife, )
    ablation (Focus ion beam, laser)

Laure
16th October 2019

I have created them but as I am no expert, does it work?

Martin: IMHO not a generally used term. See FIB (Ablation), Sectioning
Christos: Diff between sectining and thinning: sectioning removes. But results otherwise same.
M &amp; C: Terminology is not (yet) standardised around these

Let&apos;s get back to it with definitions and relations, ...</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Sample thinning</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


