        <skos:editorialNote>Meli says NIMS normally uses DI on other molecules than silicon. But DIOS imaging is the first and special case of NIMS. Wikipedia article agrees.</skos:editorialNote>
        <skos:editorialNote>RELATED: DIOS-MS is only related, not superconcept. And we should have the Related term &quot;Desorption/ionisation on silicon (DIOS)&quot;, if and only if we don&apos;t have the separate concept of DIOS-MS.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>
    


