        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A multiplexed fluorescence in-situ hybridization (FISH) imaging technique that detects the spatial positions of multiple DNA target segments across the genome, enabling computational reconstruction of the three-dimensional conformation of chromatin fibers within the nucleus in single cells.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
